Think about the historic firefox-NYT-add-fund. 
They made it up to about 100,000$ in some weeks.

BUT remeber:

- there is excelent public relations and marketing done at mozilla.org 
  and spreadfirefox.org.

- the web browser is the most often used piece of software, end users 
  of all kinds an operation systems use AND ARE AWARE OF using it. 
  Reiser4 on the other hand is a Linux only thing and filesystems 
  in general are transparent to most users.

- I'm sure the firefox campaign did benefit from both the browser war 
  as well the Windows vs Linux war in large parts.

- I would NOT expect such an event to be repeated easily.

Nevertheless, it could be worth trying but by no means 
in a halfhearted way.


